plugin: shell
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::miscellanea
id: oem-miscellanea/checkbox-provider-oem-smoke-test
estimated_duration: 0.1
command:
  echo "checkbox-provider-oem is alive and jobs are discoverable"
_summary: Confirm checkbox-provider-oem jobs are discoverable and runnable
_description:
  Trivial sanity job to confirm the checkbox-provider-oem provider is
  installed correctly and its jobs can be discovered and executed on
  Core, Desktop, and Server test plans.

plugin: shell
category_id: com.canonical.plainbox::miscellanea
id: oem-miscellanea/hello-misc
estimated_duration: 0.1
command: hello_misc.sh
_summary: Example job calling a script from a bin/ category subfolder
_description:
  Example job showing that bin/ scripts can be organized into category
  subfolders (mirroring the units/ layout), e.g. bin/miscellanea/. The
  script is discovered recursively by checkbox, but is still invoked
  here by its basename only ("hello_misc.sh"), since job execution
  looks it up on PATH rather than by its subfolder path.
